      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When the failure seems intentionally evasive, it often points toward a systemic interaction we haven't modeled yet, rather than a single component failure. In my experience, this \"mischievous\" behavior is usually a complex interplay of subtle environmental factors, like thermal expansion causing minute changes in wire resistance that only manifest under peak load. It's less about malice and more about the sheer chaotic nature of materials under stress. You might need to introduce environmental stress testing—like cycling the temperature or applying vibration *while* monitoring the sensor—to force the elusive culprit into the open.",
